# Act 2, chapter 5 "Siblings": the district around West City (areas from log4/gen_ch5.py, world 4). The Red Fangs, a
# street gang, have moved into the twins' hideout (the old warehouse at the docks); a man in a long coat paid them to.
# Flags: 293 vendor, 294 Big Ox beaten (his death script), 295 stash recovered, 296 medal returned, 297 riverside cache,
# 298 delivery returned, 299 docks cache, 387 curator asked, 388 clerk asked, 389 den intro.
list ch5_vendor
if_flag 295 vendor_after
if_flag 293 vendor_again
set_flag 293
narrate Street vendor: You two! Keep walking, before those Red Fang creeps see you talking to me.
say lapis.1 Red Fangs? Since when does that bunch of losers run the circus lot?
narrate Street vendor: Since last week. They take a cut of every sale. And last night they moved into the old warehouse down at the docks.
say lazuli.0 The warehouse. Our warehouse.
say lapis.2 Everything we own is in there.
narrate Street vendor: Then you can kiss it goodbye. Their boss is a mountain called Big Ox. Out past the river, on the island by the docks.
say lazuli.3 Big Ox. Of course he is.
journal Take back the warehouse from the {c07}Red Fangs{c02}
stop
label vendor_again
narrate Street vendor: The docks are south of the city, over the river. Big Ox doesn't leave the warehouse.
stop
label vendor_after
narrate Street vendor: You ran the Red Fangs out? Ha! First good day I've had all month. The lemonade's on me. Just this once.
list ch5_den
set_flag 389
set_flag 293
narrate The old warehouse. Their mattresses have been thrown in a heap. Someone has spray-painted a red fang on the wall.
narrate Big Ox: Well, well. The little pickpockets came home.
say lapis.1 You're in our place, Ox. Get out.
narrate Big Ox: Your place? Funny. A man paid me good money to take it off you. Said to wait here and see what you'd do.
say lazuli.0 What man?
narrate Big Ox: Doesn't matter. Boys! Teach these two some manners.
journal Defeat {c07}Big Ox{c02}
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch5_stash
if_flag 295 stash_done
unless_flag 294 stash_guarded
set_flag 295
narrate Behind the crates, under a loose board: the twins' tin box. Still there.
say lapis.2 Every zeni. They didn't even find it.
narrate Next to it, a crate the Red Fangs filled with their haul: Z-Mart cartons, and a medal in a glass case.
say lazuli.0 Somebody's going to want those back.
narrate Big Ox (from the floor): Old guy... long coat. Paid in cash. Said you two were... special. That's all I know. I swear.
say lazuli.3 Lapis. The man in the coat again.
say lapis.1 Then let him watch. We're done hiding from him.
do call 129 11 1; call 129 2 2
narrate Got a Senzu Bean and two Sodas. The stolen goods are with the twins now.
journal Head back to West City
run ch5_check
stop
label stash_guarded
narrate The stash is back here. But not with Big Ox standing over it.
stop
label stash_done
narrate Nothing left behind the crates.
list docks_dome
if_flag 299 dome_done
set_flag 299
narrate The dome house is locked. Lazuli picks the lock in four seconds.
narrate Inside: a Red Fang lookout's stash. A carton of milk and a cherry soda.
do call 129 0 1; call 129 4 1
stop
label dome_done
narrate The lookout's dome is empty now.
list cache_river
if_flag 297 river_empty
set_flag 297
narrate A rowboat pulled up under the trees. In the bottom, a forgotten thermos of tea.
do call 129 1 1
stop
label river_empty
narrate An old rowboat. Nothing else.
# ---------- Z-Mart (flag 388 asked, 298 done)
list zmart_clerk
if_flag 298 clerk_done
unless_flag 295 clerk_ask
set_flag 298
narrate Z-Mart clerk: Our delivery! The Red Fangs took it right off the truck. Where did you find this?
say lapis.2 Lying around. Some people just leave things anywhere.
narrate Z-Mart clerk: Well... thank you. Take these, on the house. And hey, if you ever need a job...
say lazuli.1 We'll pass.
do call 129 3 2
narrate Got two Vanilla Sodas.
stop
label clerk_ask
set_flag 388
narrate Z-Mart clerk: Sorry, we're nearly out of everything. The Red Fangs hijacked our delivery truck yesterday.
narrate Z-Mart clerk: And someone took three watches off the counter this morning. Kids these days.
say lapis.2 Shocking.
stop
label clerk_done
narrate Z-Mart clerk: Welcome to Z-Mart! You two again? ...Did you just put something in your pocket?
# ---------- West City Museum (flag 387 asked, 296 done)
list museum_curator
if_flag 296 curator_done
unless_flag 295 curator_ask
set_flag 296
narrate Curator: The medal! The Red Ribbon Army's own service medal, back in its case. I could kiss you both.
say lazuli.3 Please don't.
narrate Curator: Then take this. Old army rations... the soldiers swore by them.
do call 129 11 1
narrate Got a Senzu Bean.
stop
label curator_ask
set_flag 387
narrate Curator: Welcome to the West City Museum. I'm afraid our best piece is missing: a Red Ribbon Army service medal.
narrate Curator: A gang broke in two nights ago. The police say it's "not a priority". Hmph.
stop
label curator_done
narrate Curator: Every school class in West City comes to see that medal. Thanks to you, it's still here.
list museum_exhibit
narrate The Red Ribbon Army exhibit. Uniforms, a rusted rifle, a photograph of a burned-out headquarters.
narrate The plaque reads: "Destroyed in a single day. The army's chief scientist was never found."
say lazuli.0 Somebody built all this... and one kid knocked it down.
say lapis.1 Never found, huh? Bet he's somewhere sulking about it.
